  fallbackHintText: No new hint for now. Keep what worked, and change only one thing on your next try.
  progressiveHintRules:
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_SandGinger_Ratio
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Use the Large amount for sand ginger so it remains the strongest ginger flavor.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_CoarseSalt_Ratio
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: "Recall the earlier salt lesson: use the Very Small amount for coarse salt."
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_Scallion_Ratio
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Use the Small amount for scallion white so it stays fresh without overtaking the ginger.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_Ginger_Combination
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: "Sand ginger and ginger belong in the same first batch; do not press New Batch between them."
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_Scallion_Combination
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Keep scallion white in its own batch so its fresh aroma is not buried by the ginger.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_CoarseSalt_Combination
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Keep coarse salt in a separate final batch rather than adding it to the ginger group.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_CoarseSalt_Order
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Finish with coarse salt. Its Very Small amount should support the completed sauce.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_Ginger_Order
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Begin with sand ginger, then add ginger to the same first batch.
  - ruleId: L11_Hint_Scallion_Order
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: After the ginger batch, add scallion white in its own batch. Coarse salt comes last.
